 Second setting (ADR-0734 D1, 2026-09-28): `library`, where the library lives, `local` by default or `cloudsql` with the Cloud SQL instance's connection name (project:region:instance) and the Google account to sign in as: `storytree settings set library cloudsql <instance> <user>`, or `storytree settings set library local`. Stored in the same file as `{ "location": "cloudsql", "instance": …, "user": … }`. Routing (capability 1) reads it to say where a project's library is; the app (the app story's lifecycle) reads it to decide whether to start its local Postgres at all.
 
+
+As built: Settings in the app’s gear mounts the agent link’s panel through @storytree/agent-link/view. It lists every reading with its value, meaning and default or set-by-you source, and saves through capability 10’s existing writers over desktop IPC. Context guidance uses a numeric text field; Library offers local or Cloud SQL with its instance and account fields. Refusals appear inline verbatim; a read failure offers Retry, and closing returns keyboard focus to the gear. Evidence and owner-review captures: packages/agent-link/evidence/settings-panel/. Appearance awaits the owner’s acceptance.

